Hello Jim,

Thanks for the help.
I`m working with 14 models, where I allowed Psi_initial, Extinction and Colonization to be a function of elevation.

Here is the structure of one of my models:

fm13=colext(~Elev+I(Elev^2),~year-1*Elev+I(Elev^2)*Transect,~year-1*Elev+I(Elev^2)*Transect,~year,umf).
Call:
colext(psiformula = ~Elev + I(Elev^2), gammaformula = ~year -
    1 * Elev + I(Elev^2) * Transect, epsilonformula = ~year -
    1 * Elev + I(Elev^2) * Transect, pformula = ~year, data = umf)

Initial:
            Estimate    SE      z P(>|z|)
(Intercept)    0.326 0.433  0.754 0.45103
Elev           2.080 0.974  2.135 0.03276
I(Elev^2)     -2.711 0.960 -2.825 0.00472

Colonization:
                         Estimate    SE      z P(>|z|)
year2015                     32.8  75.4  0.435   0.663
year2016                     32.8  75.5  0.435   0.664
I(Elev^2)                  -263.0 604.7 -0.435   0.664
TransectToro                -35.7  75.5 -0.474   0.636
TransectTW                  204.7 286.9  0.713   0.476
TransectYunque              -33.9  75.5 -0.449   0.653
I(Elev^2):TransectToro      263.3 604.7  0.435   0.663
I(Elev^2):TransectTW       -276.8 605.1 -0.457   0.647
I(Elev^2):TransectYunque    261.1 604.7  0.432   0.666

Extinction:
                         Estimate       SE       z P(>|z|)
year2015                   -1.090    0.917 -1.1891   0.234
year2016                    0.128    0.971  0.1322   0.895
I(Elev^2)                   0.394    0.995  0.3961   0.692
TransectToro             -347.800 1130.947 -0.3075   0.758
TransectTW                 -0.668    1.130 -0.5907   0.555
TransectYunque            258.697 1033.242  0.2504   0.802
I(Elev^2):TransectToro    203.828  962.897  0.2117   0.832
I(Elev^2):TransectTW        0.963    4.782  0.2013   0.840
I(Elev^2):TransectYunque   40.555  868.858  0.0467   0.963

Detection:
            Estimate    SE      z  P(>|z|)
(Intercept)    1.127 0.187  6.039 1.55e-09
year2016      -0.504 0.275 -1.834 6.66e-02
year2019      -0.138 0.242 -0.571 5.68e-01

AIC: 733.4629

So, with this model, I can obtain the elevation profile for the first year, and for the different transects.
I`m a little lost about the next steps that you and Alex are suggesting. Should I take the estimated values of Extinction and Colonization across the elevational gradient to calculate Psi at each site and year using this formula?

psi_t = (psi_t-1 x (1 - ext_t-1)) + (col_t-1 x (1 - psi_t-1))

Thanks, and sorry if I`m missing something obvious.

Best

Marconi

On Fri, Jun 7, 2019 at 11:16 AM Jim Baldwin <jbald...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Please ignore if this is stating the obvious.  To "compare the elevation profile among the three years" you'll need to construct (explicitly) the associated "elevation profile" effect using the parameters in your model.  You'll then need to estimate the precision of that effect either using the Delta Method using the estimated covariance matrix from the colext output or  using a bootstrap.  Comparing the elevation profile among the three years is certainly a legitimate objective.  It just needs to be made explicit in terms of the parameters in the model.  That's the hard part.  Estimating the precision will be the easy (or at least easier) part.  I say all of this without a specific example because I don't see where you've given the model you're using.  (I'm reluctant to guess at the model just from the data frame you've presented.)
