Thanks Jim,

You are correct. I have two years prior to the hurricane (2015 and 2016) and one year after (2019).

I`ll really appreciate any help to re-parameterize the model so that I can have intercepts and elevation coefficients to change with year using the colext framework. I think that this should be the model structure, right?

colext(psiformula = ~Elev + I(Elev^2) * year, gammaformula = ~year - 1 * Elev + I(Elev^2) * Transect, epsilonformula = ~year -1 * Elev + I(Elev^2) * Transect, pformula = ~year, data = umf)

But I can't figure out how to proceed to be able to run this model... Should I reorganize my matrix data, so that I repeat the 68 sampling sites in the rows ( so that I will have 204 sampling sites), and identify the years by using 0,1 and NAs?

Any help is highly appreciated.

Thanks

Best,

Marconi

